/-!
# Polynomial algebras over Noetherian Cohen–Macaulay rings

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 00ND (lemma-CM-polynomial-algebra), the ring case
of Tag 0AAI (lemma-maximal-CM-polynomial-algebra)
(blueprint: lem-trf-polynomial-algebra-cm).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace MvPolynomial

/-- A polynomial ring in finitely many variables over a Noetherian ring whose prime
localizations have depth equal to dimension is Noetherian, and its prime localizations
also have depth equal to dimension.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 00ND (lemma-CM-polynomial-algebra), following the
polynomial induction of Tag 0AAI (lemma-maximal-CM-polynomial-algebra)
(blueprint: lem-trf-polynomial-algebra-cm).

Proof, following the node's ten steps:
1. Induct on `n`. For `n = 0`, identify the polynomial ring with `R`. For the successor
   step put `A = R[x₁, …, xₙ]` and identify the next polynomial ring with `B = A[X]`.
2. By induction `A` is Noetherian and has the depth equality at all primes. The finite-type
   algebra Noetherianity theorem (lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian, Tag 00FN)
   makes `B` Noetherian, using its presentation `A[X]/(0)`.
3. The monomial basis `1, X, X², …` makes `B` free over `A`, hence flat by
   lem-weil-pbc-projective-module-flat.
4. For a prime `q` of `B`, let `p` be its contraction to `A`. By
   lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-ring-maps the map `A_p → B_q` is flat and local, with
   Noetherian source and target. By lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-depth-formula its closed
   fibre `F = B_q/pB_q` is Noetherian local with the indicated quotient maximal ideal.
5. Put `D = A/p`, `W = A ∖ p`, and `k = κ(p) = Frac(D)`. Reduction gives `B/pB = D[X]`.
   Inverting `W` gives `k[X]`; let `Q = W⁻¹(q/pB)` be its prime. Then `F ≃ k[X]_Q`:
   coefficient reduction sends the class of `f/g` to its reduced fraction, and the inverse
   sends coefficient fractions to their classes in `F`. Clearing denominators in `W`
   shows every polynomial outside `Q` becomes a unit; these maps are inverse on fractions.
   In particular, `Q` is taken after inverting `W`, not directly in `D[X]`.
6. By lem-pur-polynomial-field-pid, `k[X]` is a principal ideal domain. If `Q = 0`, then
   `F = k(X)` is a field. Otherwise write `Q = (h)` with `h ≠ 0`. For any `(g) ⊇ (h)`,
   write `h = gu`; primality gives `g ∈ (h)` or `u ∈ (h)`. The first gives equality and
   the second makes `g` a unit by cancellation. Thus `Q` is maximal, and `F` is a local
   domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the nonzero nonunit `h/1`.
7. In the field case, the only prime is zero, so dimension is zero. The empty regular
   sequence is the only possible length in its zero maximal ideal, so depth is zero too.
8. Otherwise lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-maximal-localization-dimension (Tag 00OP),
   in one variable, gives dimension one. The singleton `h/1` is regular and in the
   maximal ideal, so depth is at least one. Apply lem-weil-pbc-depth-le-support-dimension
   to `F` as a module over itself: its support is the full spectrum, so depth is at most
   one. Consequently the fibre has depth and dimension `δ`, where `δ` is zero or one.
9. By lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-depth-formula (Tag 0337), the target depth is the source
   depth plus `δ`. By lem-weil-pbc-flat-height-formula (Tag 00ON), the target dimension
   is the source dimension plus `δ`. Induction identifies the source depth and dimension,
   so the target depth and dimension agree.
10. Since `q` was arbitrary, this proves the successor step and the result for all `n`.
    If `R` is zero then its polynomial rings are zero and have no primes, so the local
    assertion is vacuous; no nontriviality hypothesis on `R` is needed.
-/
theorem isNoetherianRing_and_local_depth_eq_dimension {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (hCM : ∀ (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime],
      (IsLocalRing.depth (R := Localization.AtPrime p)
        (Localization.AtPrime p) : WithBot ℕ∞) =
          ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime p))
    (n : ℕ) :
    IsNoetherianRing (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R) ∧
      ∀ (q : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R)) [q.IsPrime],
        (IsLocalRing.depth (R := Localization.AtPrime q)
          (Localization.AtPrime q) : WithBot ℕ∞) =
            ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
  sorry

end MvPolynomial
